next:
  cybertrain db migrate
  cybertrain server      # then open the /setup?token=... link it prints, on this machine (or: spin run club -- user EMAIL)
  cybertrain spin test   # test/authentication.rb, admin.rb, remember_me.rb, lockout.rb, passwords.rb and accounts.rb; snapshot them from the binaries
  # password reset mails: set CLUB_BASE_URL and CYBERTRAIN_SMTP_* (config/app.rb, Cybertrain::Config)
ok   --invite-only writes the user command and /setup instead of the sign-up page
ok   --invite-only's screens go through t, with keys the bundled dictionaries have
ok   --invite-only requires the command in bin/<app>.rb and declares setup_open
ok   --invite-only's /setup answers only to loopback with the one-time token while no user exists
ok   --invite-only's user command reads the password from stdin when not given
ok   the user command clears a lock when it sets a password
ok   the user command is written in both modes with admin and unadmin
